#{[{:activity/course {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046644} :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186506621} :activity/id #uuid "acf80487-30da-5578-b5d8-3413af242da3" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049381 :topic/id #uuid "f0242aed-46fd-5f2e-bcc2-49ee070cdccf" :topic/math-academy-id 3190} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186506606 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186506573 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4faa0bc1-0f83-5df5-b327-6631924a3461" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "e^{3t}-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506046}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186506046} :answer-field/id #uuid "29a780d4-7f5e-5121-9749-f435d4e070d4" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506399} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "82f32ceb-ba57-523c-9952-b5724c0a4bf7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3e^{2t}-2e^{3t}+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506138}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186506138} :answer-field/id #uuid "31d556ca-1ce9-5f66-b4a1-85148a156058" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506404}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "a2d20627-2f13-5baa-ae6b-0096d23c5fcc" :question/math-academy-id "q-333135" :question/problem "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=2{x}_{1}(t)-2{x}_{2}(t)-8 \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=3{x}_{2}(t)+9,\\end{aligned}\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform to both sides of each equation in our system, we get a transformed system with the solution \n\n$$\n{X}_{1}(s)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}=\\frac{3}{s-2}-\\frac{2}{s-3}+\\frac{1}{s},\\,{X}_{2}(s)=L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}=\\frac{1}{s-3}-\\frac{3}{s}.\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the original initial value problem.\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"35px\" rowspan=\"2\">$x(t)=\\,\\,$</td>\n<td height=\"40px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" rowspan=\"2\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td height=\"35px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "To find ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ satisfying the original initial value problem, we apply the inverse Laplace transform to ${X}_{1}(s)$ and ${X}_{2}(s):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) & ={L}^{-1}\\{{X}_{1}(s)\\} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{3}{s-2}-\\frac{2}{s-3}+\\frac{1}{s}\\} \\\\  & =3\\,{L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s-2}\\}-2\\,{L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s-3}\\}+{L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s}\\} \\\\  & =3{e}^{2\\cdot t}-2{e}^{3\\cdot t}+1 \\\\  & =-2{e}^{3t}+3{e}^{2t}+1 \\\\ {x}_{2}(t) & ={L}^{-1}\\{{X}_{2}(s)\\} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s-3}-\\frac{3}{s}\\} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s-3}\\}-3\\,{L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s}\\} \\\\  & ={e}^{3\\cdot t}-3 \\\\  & ={e}^{3t}-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write down the solution to the initial value problem:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-2{e}^{3t}+3{e}^{2t}+1 \\\\ {e}^{3t}-3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "1354470f-5d1a-53f8-82af-628f52a8a45f"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186506621 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167188 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "446d2e37-da3b-5ec4-9e85-ed0778e2a047" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{{s}^{2}+s-3}{s(s-1)(s-3)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506026}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186506026} :answer-field/id #uuid "ea6e246f-4955-529f-bde2-787eeb20b921" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164154}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "25f77b6f-c4e6-577f-be11-94654e67ed25" :question/math-academy-id "q-330955" :question/problem "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)={x}_{1}(t)+3 \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=-{x}_{1}(t)+3{x}_{2}(t),\\end{aligned}\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform $L$ to both sides of each equation in our system, we get a system with variables ${X}_{1}(s)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}.$ In terms of the parameter $s,$ the solution of the new system is\n\n${X}_{1}(s)=\\frac{3-2s}{s(s-1)},\\,$\n${X}_{2}(s)=$ {{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "First, we compute the Laplace transforms of both sides of each equation in our system:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}L\\{{x}_{1}^{′}(t)\\}=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)+3\\} \\\\ L\\{{x}_{2}^{′}(t)\\}=L\\{-{x}_{1}(t)+3{x}_{2}(t)\\}\\end{aligned}\\,\\,\n$$\n\nUsing the derivative property of the Laplace transform, we obtain the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}sL\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}-{x}_{1}(0)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}+3L\\{1\\} \\\\ sL\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}-{x}_{2}(0)=-L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}+3L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich can be simplified to the following:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{1}(s)+2={X}_{1}(s)+\\frac{3}{s} \\\\ s{X}_{2}(s)-1=-{X}_{1}(s)+3{X}_{2}(s)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${X}_{1}(s)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\},$ and we have used the fact that $L\\{1\\}=\\frac{1}{s}.$\n\nNow, solving the first equation for ${X}_{1}(s),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{1}(s)+2 & ={X}_{1}(s)+\\frac{3}{s} \\\\ (s-1){X}_{1}(s) & =\\frac{3}{s}-2 \\\\ (s-1){X}_{1}(s) & =\\frac{3-2s}{s} \\\\ {X}_{1}(s) & =\\frac{3-2s}{s(s-1)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this in the second equation and solving for ${X}_{2}(s),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{2}(s)-1 & =-{X}_{1}(s)+3{X}_{2}(s) \\\\ (s-3){X}_{2}(s) & =1-{X}_{1}(s) \\\\ (s-3){X}_{2}(s) & =1-(\\frac{3-2s}{s(s-1)}) \\\\ (s-3){X}_{2}(s) & =\\frac{s(s-1)-3+2s}{s(s-1)} \\\\ (s-3){X}_{2}(s) & =\\frac{{s}^{2}-s-3+2s}{s(s-1)} \\\\ (s-3){X}_{2}(s) & =\\frac{{s}^{2}+s-3}{s(s-1)} \\\\ {X}_{2}(s) & =\\frac{{s}^{2}+s-3}{s(s-1)(s-3)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution of the new system  in terms of parameter $s$ is \n\n$$\n{X}_{1}(s)=\\frac{3-2s}{s(s-1)},\\,{X}_{2}(s)=\\frac{{s}^{2}+s-3}{s(s-1)(s-3)}.\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "43aab161-e695-57a7-8969-5ee8f4c6d017" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186506652}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186506630 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186506578 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ca3e6253-cb2f-51e3-a09f-722442297438" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2e^{2t}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506269}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186506269} :answer-field/id #uuid "7ca1bb4c-a167-5a9d-a3af-6cd2b38386a7" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506437} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4a5fa96f-7d32-5292-9419-4df3266355da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-e^{2t}+1+3e^{4t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506034}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186506034} :answer-field/id #uuid "8ba858c4-352a-5ccd-b2f2-ddf2cb9c2ccb" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506444}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "afb0fc7e-4ba2-590c-909f-dbefd260c961" :question/math-academy-id "q-333125" :question/problem "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=2{x}_{1}(t)+2 \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)={x}_{1}(t)+4{x}_{2}(t)-3,\\end{aligned}\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform to both sides of each equation in our system, we get a transformed system with the solution \n\n$$\n{X}_{1}(s)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}=\\frac{2}{s-2}-\\frac{1}{s},\\,{X}_{2}(s)=L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}=-\\frac{1}{s-2}+\\frac{1}{s}+\\frac{3}{s-4}.\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the original initial value problem.\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"35px\" rowspan=\"2\">$x(t)=\\,\\,$</td>\n<td height=\"40px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" rowspan=\"2\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td height=\"35px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "To find ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ satisfying the original initial value problem, we apply the inverse Laplace transform to ${X}_{1}(s)$ and ${X}_{2}(s):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) & ={L}^{-1}\\{{X}_{1}(s)\\} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{2}{s-2}-\\frac{1}{s}\\} \\\\  & =2\\,{L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s-2}\\}-{L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s}\\} \\\\  & =2{e}^{2\\cdot t}-1 \\\\  & =2{e}^{2t}-1 \\\\ {x}_{2}(t) & ={L}^{-1}\\{{X}_{2}(s)\\} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}\\{-\\frac{1}{s-2}+\\frac{1}{s}+\\frac{3}{s-4}\\} \\\\  & =-{L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s-2}\\}+{L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s}\\}+3\\,{L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s-4}\\} \\\\  & =-{e}^{2\\cdot t}+1+3{e}^{4\\cdot t} \\\\  & =3{e}^{4t}-{e}^{2t}+1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write down the solution to the initial value problem:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2{e}^{2t}-1 \\\\ 3{e}^{4t}-{e}^{2t}+1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "69795229-d4bd-5f42-bbf9-ca3a1404c6ec" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186506606}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186506652 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167189 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ac964228-37ed-5165-995d-548c80a4f24b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{t}+\\frac{3}{2}{e}^{3t}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303520} {:answer/id #uuid "c12e4719-ad23-58b9-a060-4357d834aedf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}e^t-1+\\frac{3}{2}e^{3t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506260}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186506260} :answer-field/id #uuid "20b81a8b-8f51-59ce-bf0d-1a13def57610" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304154} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "caf736de-0666-5d9b-968f-218e1f2297c1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{e}^{t}-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303701} {:answer/id #uuid "e83c20e7-16a6-544d-a4ca-f01a743529f8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "e^t-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506336}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186506336} :answer-field/id #uuid "f768c9da-81c3-54d5-8f63-a3d84cc7ca94" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304740}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "05245fe3-011d-5dbc-b60f-1afb740f2732" :question/math-academy-id "q-330958" :question/problem "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)={x}_{1}(t)+3 \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=-{x}_{1}(t)+3{x}_{2}(t),\\end{aligned}\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform to both sides of each equation in our system, we get a transformed system with the solution \n\n$$\n{X}_{1}(s)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}=\\frac{1}{s-1}-\\frac{3}{s},\\,{X}_{2}(s)=L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}=\\frac{1/2}{s-1}-\\frac{1}{s}+\\frac{3/2}{s-3}.\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the original initial value problem.\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"35px\" rowspan=\"2\">$x(t)=\\,\\,$</td>\n<td height=\"40px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" rowspan=\"2\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td height=\"35px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "To find ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ satisfying the original initial value problem, we apply the inverse Laplace transform to ${X}_{1}(s)$ and ${X}_{2}(s):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) & ={L}^{-1}\\{{X}_{1}(s)\\} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s-1}-\\frac{3}{s}\\} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s-1}\\}-3{L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s}\\} \\\\  & ={e}^{1\\cdot t}-3\\cdot 1 \\\\  & ={e}^{t}-3 \\\\ {x}_{2}(t) & ={L}^{-1}\\{{X}_{2}(s)\\} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1/2}{s-1}-\\frac{1}{s}+\\frac{3/2}{s-3}\\} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s-1}\\}-{L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s}\\}+\\frac{3}{2}{L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s-3}\\} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{1\\cdot t}-1+\\frac{3}{2}{e}^{3\\cdot t} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{t}+\\frac{3}{2}{e}^{3t}-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write down the solution to the initial value problem:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{t}-3 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}{e}^{t}+\\frac{3}{2}{e}^{3t}-1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "d17d556a-f8ce-5c71-aba6-473c775f92dd" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186506656}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186506656 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186308369 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0039aee6-98b7-59c0-8d03-5b2d50aa3e57" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{3(s+2)}{s(s-2)(s-5)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305152}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186305152} :answer-field/id #uuid "0377913c-e842-526c-a0d1-86f1c0379261" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307528}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "e3c4c091-3098-5cdd-a98e-d6a345ec5978" :question/math-academy-id "q-333070" :question/problem "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=2{x}_{1}(t)+3{x}_{2}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=5{x}_{2}(t)+2,\\end{aligned}\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform $L$ to both sides of each equation in our system, we get a system with variables ${X}_{1}(s)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}.$ In terms of the parameter $s,$ the solution of the new system is\n\n${X}_{1}(s)=$ {{field-1}},$\\,$\n${X}_{2}(s)=\\frac{s+2}{s(s-5)}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we compute the Laplace transforms of both sides of each equation in our system:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}L\\{{x}_{1}^{′}(t)\\}=L\\{2{x}_{1}(t)+3{x}_{2}(t)\\} \\\\ L\\{{x}_{2}^{′}(t)\\}=L\\{5{x}_{2}(t)+2\\}\\end{aligned}\\,\\,\n$$\n\nUsing the derivative property of the Laplace transform, we obtain the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}sL\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}-{x}_{1}(0)=2L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}+3L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\} \\\\ sL\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}-{x}_{2}(0)=5L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}+2L\\{1\\}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich can be simplified to the following:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{1}(s)-0=2{X}_{1}(s)+3{X}_{2}(s) \\\\ s{X}_{2}(s)-1=5{X}_{2}(s)+\\frac{2}{s}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${X}_{1}(s)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\},$ and we have used the fact that $L\\{1\\}=\\frac{1}{s}.$\n\nNow, solving the second equation for ${X}_{2}(s),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{2}(s)-1 & =5{X}_{2}(s)+\\frac{2}{s} \\\\ (s-5){X}_{2}(s) & =1+\\frac{2}{s} \\\\ (s-5){X}_{2}(s) & =\\frac{s+2}{s} \\\\ {X}_{2}(s) & =\\frac{s+2}{s(s-5)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this in the first equation and solving for ${X}_{1}(s)$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{1}(s) & =2{X}_{1}(s)+3{X}_{2}(s) \\\\ (s-2){X}_{1}(s) & =3{X}_{2}(s) \\\\ (s-2){X}_{1}(s) & =3(\\frac{s+2}{s(s-5)}) \\\\ {X}_{1}(s) & =\\frac{3(s+2)}{s(s-5)(s-2)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution of the new system in terms of parameter $s$ is \n\n$$\n{X}_{1}(s)=\\frac{3(s+2)}{s(s-2)(s-5)},\\,{X}_{2}(s)=\\frac{s+2}{s(s-5)}.\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "d632b05d-a89a-5460-91b8-ea467b225b71" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186506630}}] :activity/title "Solving Inhomogeneous Systems of ODEs Using Laplace Transforms" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505910}]}
